INTENDED USE AND PROHIBITED USES

EchoLens contains identifiable human speech and participant-linked demographic
metadata, collected under Stanford IRB Protocol #77233 from participants who
consented to public redistribution.

The dataset is intended for research auditing and evaluation of audio-language
models. It is NOT for speaker identification, voice biometrics, production
voice-system deployment, or treating recordings as evidence of speaker identity.
These applications are outside the scope of participant consent and are not
permitted under any license.

The demographic labels in EchoLens are self-reported and support a bounded audit
of whether audio-language models respond differently to comparable spoken requests
across demographic speech variation. Speech cues must not be interpreted as
ground-truth evidence of identity.

Participants were never asked to state names or other direct identifiers.
Do not attempt to identify, contact, or infer the legal identity of any speaker.

Participants retain the right to withdraw. On a withdrawal request the maintainers
will remove the affected recordings and issue a new version; you agree to delete
withdrawn recordings from your copies on notification.

